From ac5eeca69f370e16a8c28357946501e8d19ae13d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:49:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix customer visits count and add Gross
 Sales/Cash/Online/Receivable totals to exports

- customer_summary.total_transactions now counts distinct transaction_date
  values (excluding cancelled orders), matching how a laundry shop actually
  thinks about "a visit" - a customer with two same-day drop-offs now shows
  1 visit, not 2, and a cancelled order no longer counts as one either.
  last_visit is fixed the same way.
- The n8n transaction export (both CSV and Google Sheets output) now leads
  with 4 summary totals the owner asked for: Gross Sales, Total Cash Sales
  Received, Total Online Payments, Total Amounts Receivable. All four are
  grouped by payment_method (consistent with the existing Reports page),
  cancelled orders excluded, and Receivable nets off any cash/gcash already
  collected on a Pay Later order rather than showing its full amount. Rows
  themselves are unchanged (cancelled orders still listed, for the record)
  and now also carry an Order Status column. Google Sheets gets a new
  "Summary" tab; CSV gets the same 4 lines before the header row.
- export-transactions Edge Function now selects order_status so the n8n
  workflow can tell which rows are cancelled.
- Printable PDF report (src/lib/pdf-report.ts) relabelled its stats block to
  the same 4 totals and definitions, and picked up a real bug fix along the
  way: it previously counted cancelled orders in its sales figures (the
  Reports page already excluded them) and showed Pay Later's full amount
  instead of the true outstanding receivable when a partial payment existed.
- tests/backend/test.mjs: new pglite test for the visits-by-date/cancelled
  behavior, plus one existing assertion updated to reflect the corrected
  (lower) visit count for two same-day transactions.

Verification: check:migrations PASS, build PASS, lint PASS (0 errors, no
new warnings), git diff --check PASS, tests/backend 66+39 PASS/0 FAIL,
test:customer-items 8 PASS/0 FAIL, test:sales-metrics 12 PASS/0 FAIL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DeFV6HNfuxKwGxuKyxSEx9
